 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Sure. Complementary color is the color opposite a given color. For example, if you wear blue, the compliment would be yellow since they are opposites on the color wheel. It comes from history. Before pigments, people used pigment lakes from minerals and roots. Blue came from lapis lazuli, rare and expensive. Yes, you can. It gives a classic, high end look that's timeless. Then go ahead. Stick with the complement for the shirt, and black for the walls or furniture.",
